---
description: C++ naming, C4458, Unreal renames, and camelCase names for new Cursor rules.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Prefixes
- Classes use `JoA_` (`UJoA_UnitComponent`,
  `AJoA_Hero`), unless `gas.mdc` says otherwise.
- Enums and structs have no `JoA_` prefix.
  `EUnitType`, `FDamageInfo`.
- `A`, `U`, `F`, and `E` still apply. See `core.mdc`.

# Widgets
- A widget class uses `JoA_W_`, then the Blueprint
  name with `WBP_` removed. Keep the Unreal `U`.
- `WBP_Play` becomes `UJoA_W_Play`. The file is
  `JoA_W_Play.h` and `JoA_W_Play.cpp`.
- A widget without a Blueprint yet takes the name
  the Blueprint will get, with `WBP_` removed.
- This replaces plain `JoA_` for widgets. It does
  not apply to `JoA_GAS_` classes.

# Local names must not hide members
- A local, parameter, or lambda capture must not
  match a member of this class or a base.
  MSVC error C4458.
- `PlayerState` hides `APawn::PlayerState`.
  Use `OwnerState` for an `AJoA_PlayerState*`.
- The same covers `Owner`, `Controller`,
  `Instigator`, and `RootComponent`.

# Renames follow the class
- When a class is renamed, rename every member of
  that type in other classes.
- Rename the Get and Set functions for that member
  to the same name.
- `UJoA_GAS_CombatSet` uses `CombatSet`,
  `GetCombatSet`, and `SetCombatSet`.

# Renames that leave references
- Do not add `ClassRedirects`, `ObjectRedirects`,
  `PropertyRedirects`, or `EnumRedirects` to
  `Config/DefaultEngine.ini`.
- Tell the user the old name, the new name, and
  which assets still store the old name. Then give
  the steps for that kind of rename.

## Asset moved or renamed in Content
- Right-click the folder in the Content Browser
  and run Update Redirector References.
- That loads `UObjectRedirector` assets, resaves
  referencers onto the new asset, and can delete
  the redirectors. Save the packages it dirties.

## C++ class, property, struct, enum, or component
- Update Redirector References finds nothing.
  A C++ rename does not create a redirector.
- Recompile and restart the editor.
- Open each Blueprint that still uses the old name.
  Delete the broken component or rewire the broken
  pin, then Compile and Save.
- If the Blueprint parent class itself was renamed,
  the asset will not open. Say so and ask before
  adding a `ClassRedirect`.

# Sound file names
When the user writes `check sound`, rename every
file in `Content/Audio/SFX/`.

- Take the file name without the extension.
- If it already starts with `SFX_`, the name is
  the rest. Otherwise the name is the whole stem.
- The new stem is `SFX_` plus that name with its
  first letter capitalized.
- `cheer` becomes `SFX_Cheer`. `SFX_Jump` stays
  `SFX_Jump`.
- Rename the source file and the `.uasset` of the
  same stem together.
- Skip a file that already has that name.
- Put the renames on the numbered CL of this work.
  Do not submit.

# Cursor rule file names
- A new rule in `.cursor/rules/` uses camelCase:
  `nameName.mdc`.
- `binaryGraphicsWorkflow.mdc` is right.
  `binary-graphics-workflow.mdc` is wrong.
- One word stays one word: `naming.mdc`, `gas.mdc`.
